messages:
ash p: Quick sync — need final scope for API consolidation v0.3 before Thurs release. customers want streaming + structured output + typed function-calls examples.

devon (sdk): We can do TS + Python defs, but need to lock on the shape for structured output. two implementation paths: runtime-typed wrappers vs generated helpers.

maria-docs: For docs, prefer generated helpers — simpler examples for folks. Also want small runnable snippets for Playground.

kevin-backend: Backend constraints: streaming + function-calling tandem increases headroom. If we enable both by default, we need to flag batching behavior. Might need a fallback model for low-latency.

jess-se: Customer ask: one code path that supports both chat.completions and tool calls. They care about consistent error semantics.

ash p: Prioritization idea: Must-have (API contract + typed examples), Nice-to-have (streaming in examples), Stretch (automatic helper generation). Agree? :eyes:

devon (sdk): Agree. Proposal: ship types + simple examples in both clients. Add streaming examples in a follow-up patch. I'll draft API surface PR.

maria-docs: I'll prepare the docs checklist and example gallery entries. Need final JSON schema for structured_output by EOD Wed.

kevin-backend: Can we add a compatibility header so SDKs can detect server capability? e.g., `x-redwood-features: functions,streaming`

ash p: yes — add feature header. Launch criteria (must): 1) Types published in npm/pypi, 2) docs examples for function-calls + structured output, 3) CI tests for type-checking examples, 4) compatibility header present.

jess-se: I'll compile a short customer-facing changelog blurb and a migration note. Keep it to 3 bullets.

devon (sdk): rough TS snippet for docs — feel free to copy/edit: 
```ts
type FunctionCall = {
  name: string;
  arguments: Record<string, unknown>;
};

type StructuredOutput<T> = {
  schemaVersion: string;
  payload: T;
};

// usage
const resp: StructuredOutput<{userId: string}> = await client.callFunction('get-user', {id: '123'});
```

maria-docs: perfect. I'll make a Python equivalent and add runnable cells.

ci-bot: deploy-preview created — https://deploy.redwood.dev/pr-1234 (staging). :white_check_mark:

ash p: Actions: devon PR for types (due Wed noon), maria docs draft (Wed EOD), kevin to add header + fallback (Thu EOD), jess churn changelog (Thu AM). If all green, we cut Friday.

devon (sdk): noted — I'll open the PR now and tag reviewers. @maria-docs @kevin-backend

maria-docs: pinged — adding checklist to the docs repo.

kevin-backend: starting feature header impl. will post perf notes if we see latency regressions.

jess-se: I'll prepare the customer comms and hand to growth.

ash p: thanks team — short sync tomorrow 10am to confirm go/no-go. :thumbsup:
